% Ring-Out (pure movement)
%
% An ogre stands on a plinth by the void. Nothing hurts it: the only way to
% win is to ring it out - over the verge. Two companions, one skill each,
% from six. The idea is Into the Breach's: the enemy never starts on a line
% into the void, so somebody moves it first. A knockback never leaves its
% area and the plinth has no edge, so a push there goes nowhere.
%
%   gate --- yard --- plinth (ogre)
%              \        /
%               brink (verge: the void)
%
% Every method is the same two steps, by two companions:
%   bring    onto the brink: stand there and hook it over from the plinth;
%            or stand there and taunt it - it walks after you and slams the
%            brink where it arrives (a heavy physical blow: everyone else
%            there is stunned and knocked, maybe over the verge)
%   knock    over the verge: a fireball (from the gate or the yard), a
%            shield bash (from next door), a tidal wave (standing on the
%            brink), or a vortex on the verge (it takes everyone there)
% The slam is answered - a friend knocks the ogre over in the window and it
% misses - or taken: sacrifice is allowed. Whoever stands on the brink may
% step back into the yard first (a taunter who does leads the ogre along).
%
% Traps: two knockers only shove it about on the plinth; a bringer alone
% brings it and no further; a vortex on the verge or a wave on the brink
% takes the friend still standing there.

% === Map: four areas ===
region(gate).
region(yard).
region(brink).
region(plinth).
connected(gate, yard).
connected(yard, brink).
connected(yard, plinth).
connected(brink, plinth).

lineOfSight(gate, yard).
lineOfSight(gate, brink).
lineOfSight(yard, gate).
lineOfSight(yard, brink).
lineOfSight(yard, plinth).
lineOfSight(brink, yard).
lineOfSight(brink, plinth).
lineOfSight(plinth, yard).
lineOfSight(plinth, brink).

% === Features ===
% The brink ends at the void; the plinth has no edge on it.
feature(brink, verge, chasm).

% === Companions ===
role(player, player).
role(mage, companion).
at(player, gate).
at(mage, gate).
mana(player, 4).
mana(mage, 4).

% === The ogre ===
role(ogre, enemy).
at(ogre, plinth).
tag(ogre, living).
behavior(ogre, taunted, groundSlam, here).

% === Default kit (a winning pair; combos strips these) ===
knows(player, fireball).
knows(mage, hook).

% === Victory: ring it out ===
win :- if(), do(bringTo(ogre, brink, none), stepBack, finish(ogre)).

% Whoever stands on the brink may stay, or step back into the yard (a
% taunter who steps back leads the ogre off the brink again).
stepBack :- if(), do().
stepBack :- if(first(onBrink(?a))), do(allBack).
allBack :- allOf, if(onBrink(?a)), do(walkTo(?a, yard)).
onBrink(?a) :- at(?a, brink), canAct(?a), not(gone(?a)), not(forbidden(?a, move)).

% Already over (knocked in while it wound up its slam), or knocked in now.
finish(?e) :- if(neutralized(?e)), do().
finish(?e) :-
    if(not(neutralized(?e))), do(knockOn(?e, feature(verge), none), confirmStopped(?e)).

funExpect(single_actor_plans, atMost, 0).

% === Choice: one skill each, from six (htn_components combos) ===
comboSeat(player, 1).
comboSeat(mage, 1).
comboPool(fireball).
comboPool(tidalWave).
comboPool(shieldBash).
comboPool(vortex).
comboPool(hook).
comboPool(taunt).

goals(win).
